infiltrator-software (0.3.95) unstable; urgency=high

  * Route pure-removal final-state validation through the canonical dependency
    resolver, eliminating a weaker duplicate interpreter whose Multi-Arch rules
    could approve an invalid retained package set.
  * Make deb822 source syntax one shared authority for inventory, mutation and
    native repository configuration while preserving inline Signed-By armour
    and rejecting malformed or duplicate trust-sensitive fields.
  * Remove the dpkg architecture-query subprocess from native reconciliation by
    reading and validating dpkg's persisted architecture registry directly.
  * Remove retired Installed fallback state, report engine failures as explicit
    partial/unavailable state, and surface Flatpak inventory filesystem errors.
  * Make the installed D-Bus interface XML the single protocol-schema authority
    and generate the service's embedded introspection data from that exact file.
  * Add focused Multi-Arch removal regressions and strengthen architecture and
    documentation contracts around the consolidated ownership boundaries.
  * Complete a repository-wide forensic pass: remove stale dual-source state,
    consolidate GUI subprocess construction and user history-path ownership,
    and correct catalogue-cache handling of Common's errno-style atomic writer.
  * Fail closed on Cinnamon Spice HTTPS redirects, advance the exact Common pin
    to 1.19.42, and align maintained state/package documentation with reality.
  * Remove the obsolete self-modifying forensic repair workflow and make the
    single permanent CI/release workflow an executable repository contract.
  * Remove duplicated Common-version prose and retired backend terminology so
    the gitlink and current engine/service boundaries remain the only truths.

